<Base title="Shell recipes" description="The tools you already have, piped into ThinkThen.">
  <h1>Shell recipes</h1>
  <p class="lede">The tools you already have, piped into ThinkThen.</p>

  <p>No new function, and nothing bundled. The ten functions are right. A common tool needs one <code>jq</code> line in front and one behind, and those two lines are the recipe. The trick that makes every recipe work already ships: <code>--jsonl</code> reads one JSON row per record, <code>--field</code> names the part the model sees, and the row that comes back is <code>{'{"input": <the whole row>, "value": <the answer>}'}</code>. Paths, line numbers, dates, and ids ride through untouched and never reach the model.</p>

  <div class="note">The recipes follow. Each one is recorded first, and the page then shows the run. Nothing is written here until it has run.</div>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/tutorial/">Tutorial</a> · <a href="/reference/">Reference</a> · <a href="/how-tos/">How-tos</a></p>
</Base>
